      "title": "Revisit ralph wrap-up agent design and test coverage",
      "description": "PR #369 added a wrap-up agent that runs on ralph loop exit. Retrospective flagged it as over-engineered but the intent is broader than simple cleanup: it ensures all work is completed, finds in-progress work where task state doesn't match reality, root-causes whether work is still needed, and does best-effort to get the project into a clean state (either continue the loop or put work on a branch with a task for the user). Too many possible states to rely on code alone — the agent approach is intentional. However: runWrapUpAgent() has zero integration tests (all 37 tests only check prompt strings and boolean helpers). Revisit AC coverage, add integration tests for the actual agent spawn/timeout/cleanup paths, and verify the prompt adequately covers the intended scenarios.",
